Subject: [file-sql 1/2] sql parser: read_csv/read_json/read_ndjson/read_parquet/glob as table factors

Adds the SQL surface for competition task 2 ("文件即数据库"): the five file
table functions accepted in FROM, their "name = value" option list, and the
three new parse-node item types.

Grammar only - nothing consumes the new node types yet, so ordinary SQL is
unchanged.  The names go into unreserved_keyword_normal, so existing
statements that use read_csv / glob / header / sample_size as an identifier
keep parsing (spec: 不得破坏现有普通 SQL).

The argument shape is deliberately strict: one positional path plus
"key = value" options only.  That is what makes
    select * from read_csv('a.csv', 'xml')
fail in the parser with ER_PARSE_ERROR (1064) while
    select * from read_csv('a.csv', sample_size = 10)
parses and is left for the resolver to reject with OB_NOT_SUPPORTED (1235),
matching file_sql_basic.test:23-26.  OB_ERR_PARSER_SYNTAX would map to 1149,
not 1064, so the rejection genuinely has to come from bison.

Option values use conf_const rather than INTNUM because sample_size must
accept -1: INTNUM alone cannot carry a minus sign (cf. the "'-' INTNUM"
alternative of conf_const, sql_parser_mysql_mode.y:1118).

Option keys reuse the existing external_file_format nonterminal
(sql_parser_mysql_mode.y:7294-7370), so FIELD_DELIMITER / ESCAPE /
FIELD_OPTIONALLY_ENCLOSED_BY / ENCODING / COMPRESSION / NULL_IF_EXETERNAL
etc. come for free; only HEADER, SAMPLE_SIZE and FORMAT are new.

NOT COMPILED AND NOT BISON-CHECKED.  bison/flex/win_flex_bison are all absent
on the machine this was drafted on, and deps/3rd does not exist.  Before
merging, run the check the repo already automates:
    win_bison -v -Wno-deprecated -Wno-other -d sql_parser_mysql_mode.y \
              -o out.c --report-file=out.report
(that is exactly src/sql/parser/gen_parser_win.ps1:27, which treats any
output matching "conflict" as fatal).  Watch HEADER/SAMPLE_SIZE/FORMAT
against the pre-existing "explain_or_desc FORMAT COMP_EQ format_name" (:12300)
and "SHOW TRACE FORMAT COMP_EQ STRING_VALUE" (:12740).  Note the Linux
generator pins bison to 2.4.1 (src/sql/parser/gen_parser.sh:33-38), so a
clean run on a newer win_bison still wants one confirmation on 2.4.1.

NULLSTR is registered but not yet used by any production - it belongs to the
COPY patch.  Drop the NULLSTR lines if that is a problem for your build.

